                            	  1972: 
                            	  1973:                 ; Timestamp: PTM TIMER 3, read MSB then LSB because reading
                            	  1974:                 ; the MSB latches the LSB.  T3 rather than T1 because on
                            	  1975:                 ; the panic image the RTOS has ALREADY programmed it --
                            	  1976:                 ; latch $27C7 = (4*10-1)<<8 | (800/4-1), dual 8-bit, giving
                            	  1977:                 ; a 10.0000 ms tick at E = 800 kHz -- so the tap needs no
                            	  1978:                 ; PTM writes at all in the configuration that matters, and
                            	  1979:                 ; it reads the very counter the firmware's own sub-tick
                            	  1980:                 ; clock reads (TRAP #0 $1C at $F00F96).  On the --reset
                            	  1981:                 ; image T3 is unprogrammed and this column reads a
                            	  1982:                 ; constant, which is self-evidently not a timestamp; `s+`
                            	  1983:                 ; starts it there.
01:00F0B828 123900F7000D    	  1984:                 move.b  $F7000D,d1
01:00F0B82E E149            	  1985:                 lsl.w   #8,d1
01:00F0B830 123900F7000F    	  1986:                 move.b  $F7000F,d1
