01:00F0B8A2 4CDF0307        	  2021:                 movem.l (sp)+,d0-d2/a0-a1
                            	  2022:                 ; rts pops the target we just pushed and jumps to it,
                            	  2023:                 ; leaving the exception frame below it untouched for the
                            	  2024:                 ; original handler's own rte.  MON_TAPTGT is a single
                            	  2025:                 ; global slot, so this is not re-entrant -- which is safe
                            	  2026:                 ; here because all four channel BIMs are programmed to
                            	  2027:                 ; $5F, level 7, and a 68000 masks the level it is already
                            	  2028:                 ; servicing.  Two channel taps cannot nest.
01:00F0B8A6 2F390000F8D4    	  2029:                 move.l  MON_TAPTGT,-(sp)
01:00F0B8AC 4E75            	  2030:                 rts
                            	  2031: .own:
01:00F0B8AE 4CDF0307        	  2032:                 movem.l (sp)+,d0-d2/a0-a1
01:00F0B8B2 4E73            	  2033:                 rte
                            	  2034: 
                            	  2035: ;================================================================
                            	  2036: ; TIER 5 — the bulk path, the chassis window and the ready flag
                            	  2037: ;
                            	  2038: ;   e [NN]      drain NN words from the bulk data port
                            	  2039: ;   p PP [NN]   read NN longs from chassis page PP
                            	  2040: ;   q           bounded poll of $FF0004 bit 0
                            	  2041: ;
                            	  2042: ; --- e ---
                            	  2043: ; Reproduces TCBRDHC's polled bulk loop at $F04AE2: arm
                            	  2044: ; XLTR_STATUS_IRQ ($FF0218) with $400 — bit 10, the arm — poll bit 15
                            	  2045: ; for done, clear, then `move.w (a0),(a1)+` with a0 = $FF0008.  The
                            	  2046: ; firmware writes XLTR_COUNTER ($FF020C) = 4 when the bulk port is the
                            	  2047: ; source, which is the concrete role of that register.
                            	  2048: ;
                            	  2049: ; It reads $FF0000 BEFORE and AFTER the drain, because that is the one
                            	  2050: ; SBC-visible test of whether the word count is a hardware down-counter.
                            	  2051: ; The firmware only ever COMPARES that register — three cmpi, never a
                            	  2052: ; move — and never writes it, while its value decreases as the FIFO is
                            	  2053: ; popped; and the AP I/F photograph carries six 74S169 synchronous
                            	  2054: ; UP/DOWN counters against three up-only parts.  Firmware evidence and
                            	  2055: ; silicon agree and neither was derived from the other.  If the count
                            	  2056: ; does not fall, either the port is not being popped or the counter is
                            	  2057: ; not loaded — and this prints both readings so the operator can tell.
                            	  2058: ;
                            	  2059: ; --- p ---
                            	  2060: ; MODE2 ($FF0210) is the page register for the $400000 window:
                            	  2061: ; page = addr >> 20, offset = (addr & $FFFFF) << 2, so one page is 1M
                            	  2062: ; longwords and the field is 12 bits — 4096 pages, not the 4 bits the
                            	  2063: ; observed $0/$F suggest.  MODE2 is saved and restored, because the
                            	  2064: ; firmware itself saves and restores it in all four of its disciplines
                            	  2065: ; and RTOS init forces it to zero; leaving it changed would put a later
                            	  2066: ; operation on the wrong page with no path to correction.
                            	  2067: ;
                            	  2068: ; --- q ---
                            	  2069: ; All eleven $FF0004 sites in the firmware are byte-identical UNBOUNDED
                            	  2070: ; spins: move.w, btst #0, beq back, with no counter and no exit but
                            	  2071: ; success.  That makes it the hardest obligation on the board — a model
                            	  2072: ; that never raises it produces no diagnostic at all — so the one thing
                            	  2073: ; a probe must not do is reproduce the unbounded spin.  This one counts.
                            	  2074: ;================================================================
                            	  2075: cmd_bulk:
